ke bites now disappear one second  sooner needless to say riot definitely  wanted to make changes to the top tier  smoke agents now asher and viper weren't  the only ones who received updates both  omen and brim received some much needed  buffs the cooldown on omen smokes has  gone down from 40 seconds to 30 so  you'll have more opportunities to use  them as the round goes on but the  biggest change to his kit has to be the  travel time on his smokes the speed has  more than doubled from 2800 to 6400 and  these things can now fly across the map  almost instantly riot has also decreased  the cost of his teleport from 150 to 100  and lowered the pre-teleport delay from  1 second to 0.7 seconds  omen's paranoia has also been altered  slightly so we shouldn't get team  flashed as often now his smokes did go  up in price from 100 to 150 but given  the fact that they're the most important  part of his kit i think it's a pretty  fair trade-off next up we have brimstone  who i think received one of the most  interesting buffs in this entire patch  the deploy time on brim smokes has gone  down from two seconds to only one the  range on his ipad has increased from  5000 to 5500 and his smokes now match  the height of everyone else's but the  final change to brimstone is where  things get  kinda weird not only does brim's stim  beacon apply a 15 increase to your rate  of fire but it now also applies a 15  speed boost previously we saw this type  of mechanic applied in game modes like  spike rush so it'll be interesting to  see what it looks like in the real game  until then here's what the pros had to  say i'm gonna be honest i think i think  i think brimstone is better than omen  really good now i think it is i think it  really is sick  the fact that they nerfed  astra and they gave him movement speed  to his teammate like smoke down  it's pretty sick brimstone  i'll shoot hella fast liz and i tested  out brim's stim beacon with neon and no  the speed boost doesn't stack now 